      "message": "fix(chamfer): take a wall's lean from the frame, not from the sections\n\nThe #2936 exemption read the move between the top and corner sections\noff their centroids. A plate with a 1 mm bevel on one side and an equal\nundercut lip on the other side is also a moved copy of its wall, so a\nno-pick 2D Chamfer cut it all round (the defect of #2887).\n\n`wall_lean` now gives the move that the operation frame gives to an\nupright wall: zero with no frame or an upright frame. `leans` accepts\nonly that move. `partly_bevelled` also cuts each top segment at the\nfoot of each wall vertex inside it, so a side that runs past the wall\ncorner reads as its sharp length plus the overhang. Tests move to\nchamfer_ride_tests.rs (400-line law).\n\nFixes #2944\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
